From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Austin Shirley <austin@deadband.dev>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 11:30:38 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] feat(st): make BL33_CFG optional

Only add the HW_CONFIG payload when BL33_CFG is set. BL33 then uses
its own DT, e.g. U-Boot with its appended DT, which is then covered
by the BL33 hash.

Resolves failed builds caused by fiptool always taking the next option
as the HW_CONFIG file when BL33_CFG is unset.

Tested on STM32MP135.

Change-Id: Ic588cc7d580b20b1c3f3734b716190e6955d88f7
Upstream: https://review.trustedfirmware.org/q/Ic588cc7d580b20b1c3f3734b716190e6955d88f7
Signed-off-by: Austin Shirley <austin@deadband.dev>
---
 docs/plat/st/stm32mp1.rst | 6 ++++++
 plat/st/common/common.mk  | 5 ++++-
 2 files changed, 10 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/docs/plat/st/stm32mp1.rst b/docs/plat/st/stm32mp1.rst
index 39a43eebe2..917b45da8e 100644
--- a/docs/plat/st/stm32mp1.rst
+++ b/docs/plat/st/stm32mp1.rst
@@ -179,6 +179,12 @@ With OP-TEE:
         BL32_EXTRA2=<optee_directory>/tee-pageable_v2.bin
         fip
 
+``BL33_CFG`` is optional. To keep the U-Boot DT inside BL33, set
+``BL33=<u-boot_directory>/u-boot.bin`` (U-Boot with its appended DT), leave
+``BL33_CFG`` unset and remove the ``hw-config`` node from the board FW_CONFIG.
+U-Boot then uses its own DT, and the DT is covered by the BL33 hash rather than
+the HW_CONFIG one.
+
 Trusted Boot Board
 __________________
 
diff --git a/plat/st/common/common.mk b/plat/st/common/common.mk
index 0bedb72246..075bf0555b 100644
--- a/plat/st/common/common.mk
+++ b/plat/st/common/common.mk
@@ -87,8 +87,11 @@ STM32_DEPS			+=	${STM32IMAGE}
 FIP_DEPS			+=	dtbs
 STM32MP_HW_CONFIG		:=	${BL33_CFG}
 
-# Add the HW_CONFIG to FIP and specify the same to certtool
+# Add the HW_CONFIG to FIP and specify the same to certtool.
+# It is optional: without it, BL33 uses its own embedded DT.
+ifneq (${STM32MP_HW_CONFIG},)
 $(eval $(call TOOL_ADD_PAYLOAD,${STM32MP_HW_CONFIG},--hw-config))
+endif
 
 # Add the build options to pack Trusted OS Extra1 and Trusted OS Extra2 images
 # in the FIP if the platform requires.
